        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> The problem here was to compute the proper target destination and proper intermediate places. As although the line is displayed wrapped, it isn't so internally (it is still a single line). So it would need some extra work with window views which are both not trivial and might be computationally (relatively) expensive.\n\nFrom some initial brainstorming I had the idea to do just a basic calculation where you check if the cursor position's column is \ngreater than the width of the window then to do a calculation to get the displayed position rather than the internal position by subtracting the width from the column number. I am not sure exactly how this would be implemented but I hope it helps!",
